  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Services Administration obligated $20.1B in contract dollars in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration recorded 970,314 awards with an average award size of $20.7K. General Services Administration obligations fell 15.5% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows a rise from $17.7B in FY21 to a peak of $26.5B in FY24, then a decline to $23.8B in FY25 and $20.1B in FY26. Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services lead spending, with $4.2B and $3.5B respectively in FY2026 to date. Automobile Manufacturing is the third-largest category at $2.3B. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC is the top vendor at $1.7B, followed by SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $897M and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $758M. This snapshot covers contract obligations and fiscal-year-to-date totals only.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has General Services Administration contract spending changed over recent years?",
        "body": "General Services Administration obligations rose from $17.7B in FY21 to $26.5B in FY24, then declined to $23.8B in FY25 and to $20.1B in FY26. General Services Administration obligations fell 15.5% year over year between the most recent reporting periods. General Services Administration recorded 970,314 awards in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $20.7K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors account for the largest share of GSA obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services are the largest categories at $4.2B and $3.5B respectively in FY2026 to date. Automobile Manufacturing and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction follow at $2.3B and $1.2B. BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC, SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION, and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. are the top vendors at $1.7B, $897M, and $758M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
